{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/574356-majesty-humanity-questions","id":574356,"title":"Majesty & Humanity Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-30T14:39:47-07:00","id":574356,"title":"Majesty & Humanity Questions","content":"So Majesty relieves social penalties, right? Does it relieve the penalty to relate to humans that you get from having low Humanity?<br /> <br /> <br /> Other question: I like that the wording of the lower Humanity tiers was vagued up. Rather than all social rolls, it's rolls to relate to humans, right? So what kind of stuff do you generally apply it to in your games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T15:05:39-07:00","id":574413,"title":"","content":"I would say yes, it does relieve Humanity penalties <i>to Social dice pools</i>, but as you astutely observed, Humanity-based penalties apply to all rolls to interact with humans, which may include non-Social dice pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T16:52:01-07:00","id":574476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/574356-majesty-humanity-questions#post574356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Majesty relieves social penalties, right? Does it relieve the penalty to relate to humans that you get from having low Humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep. Even the Nosferatu's. The only exception I can think of would be trying to read emotions with an Wits+Empathy roll (which Auspex can do). In general, I get the impression that low Humanity penalties are easily negated via reliance on Disciplines. <br /> <br /> &quot;Also, there are minor Social modifiers listed. These modifiers apply to rolls relating to humans. Manipulating humans for food with Subterfuge or frightening them with Intimidation are not affected; but trying to understand a human\u2019s emotional cues with the Empathy Skill would be affected.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other question: I like that the wording of the lower Humanity tiers was vagued up. Rather than all social rolls, it's rolls to relate to humans, right? So what kind of stuff do you generally apply it to in your games? </div> </div> </div> I call it up anytime we're dealing with a human being, be it face to face or through texting or phone calls. I do not apply it to Mental rolls relating to humans (Int+Streetwise to know where to score drug, Wits+Politics to understand beaurocracy), or through formal letters/email (ie anything non-personal). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T13:59:23-07:00","id":586427,"title":"","content":"I think this fits with the tone of the game. Vampires become extremely reliant on their powers to even relate to humanity on a basic level, and this in turn drives vampires further and further away from viewing themselves as human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5106-umoja","name":"Umoja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T03:20:20-07:00","id":586937,"title":"","content":"I guess tossing Majesty around everytime vampires need to interact with followers and public will attrack the unwanted attention from those who can recognize supernatural effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T05:04:24-07:00","id":586983,"title":"","content":"Disciplines, for the most part, are actually designed so you won't notice them being used on you. Especially mortals, since they are the ones who suffer the social penalty from the vamp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T14:16:04-07:00","id":587415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/574356-majesty-humanity-questions?p=586937#post586937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess tossing Majesty around everytime vampires need to interact with followers and public will attrack the unwanted attention from those who can recognize supernatural effects.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, Majesty makes the user the center of attention for everyone around him, so it's not much use when a character needs interact with someone discretely. That's the biggest problem with using it casually to over come social penalties to low humanity. Typically, I'd expect a character to develop a devotion mixing Majesty 1 with Obfuscate 1, if he wants to overcome social penalties without attracting the wrong kind of attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T18:45:36-07:00","id":597636,"title":"","content":"I don't apply the humanity penalty to social rolls that aren't specifically aimed at understanding human feelings on a deep level. Bargaining for a good deal on a used car I wouldn't let it come in, for instance. For the most part I don't even let it come into seduction rolls for shallow one night stands, since that's mostly about the conquest and if vampires know how to do one thing it is how to hunt. If they wanted to turn that one night stand into something more and move into a more serious relationship, then the penalties would start happening as the other person starts noticing the cracks in the vampire's understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T12:01:38-07:00","id":602057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/574356-majesty-humanity-questions#post574356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Majesty relieves social penalties, right? Does it relieve the penalty to relate to humans that you get from having low Humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Fear the Nosferatu who develops Majesty. On the other hand, it's an unnatural means of mitigating the problem and only works from the mortals' perspective; it won't give the vampire any greater insight into the feelings of mortals. It also makes the vampire the center of attention, which is not always desirable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other question: I like that the wording of the lower Humanity tiers was vagued up. Rather than all social rolls, it's rolls to relate to humans, right? So what kind of stuff do you generally apply it to in your games? </div> </div> </div>All sorts of things. Scaring humans is easy for vampires at all levels, but actually understanding how they feel gets progressively more difficult. That extends to knowing the right thing to say to make them feel the way you want. Thus is effects all manner of rolls related to empathy, persuasion, etc. It might also impact certain uses of the Subterfuge skill that rely on understanding human psychology.<br /> <br /> What it's meant to model is that vampires gradually lose touch with how mortals think and even get to the point where they no longer have the patience to try to figure it out. At the same time, from the mortals' perspective the vampires' appearance and behavior become more subtly alien and unconsciously give them the willies. It's a vicious cycle at both ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T00:37:48-07:00","id":607548,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't allow Majesty to remove nosferatu clan bane. But others do.. so..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}